\details{
The results are read directly from the loaded Monolix project via
\code{\link[lixoftConnectors:getModelBuildingResults]{lixoftConnectors::getModelBuildingResults()}}.
Model building must already have been run for the project.

\strong{Strategy (auto-detected).} The strategy is read from
\code{\link[lixoftConnectors:getModelBuildingSettings]{lixoftConnectors::getModelBuildingSettings()}}. COSSAC and SCM build the model
one relationship at a time and the connector returns the tested relationship,
the step direction and the selected \code{bestModel}. SAMBA (\code{"covSamba"}) instead
proposes whole candidate covariate models per iteration, it has no single
nested parent and the connector returns neither \code{tested} nor \code{bestModel} (see
SAMBA note below).

\strong{Reference model and deltas.} For COSSAC/SCM each tested model's \emph{nested
parent} is the model whose covariate structure is identical except for the
single tested relationship. \code{dOFV}/\code{dBICc} are computed against that parent. In
the first forward round the parent is the model building start model, which
already reflects any covariate relationships defined in the base project. For
SAMBA the deltas are computed against the start model (\verb{Model 1}) instead.

\strong{SAMBA.} Covariate model building with SAMBA always selects by BICc. The
connector reports \code{criterion = "LRT"}, but that setting only governs
\emph{statistical} model building (not covered here), so it is ignored for
\code{"covSamba"}. Because the connector does not flag a best model, the best model
is derived as the one with the lowest BICc (\code{BestModel = "Yes"}); when SAMBA
finds no improvement this is the start model. An \code{Improved} flag reports
whether BICc decreased vs the start model. No \code{Tested}, \code{Step}, \code{p.value} or
\code{Significant} columns are produced (the candidates are not nested).

\strong{Selection criterion (auto-detected, COSSAC/SCM).} The columns adapt to the
criterion used for the run, read from
\code{\link[lixoftConnectors:getModelBuildingSettings]{lixoftConnectors::getModelBuildingSettings()}}:
\itemize{
\item \strong{LRT}: a likelihood-ratio-test \code{p.value} and a \code{Significant} flag are
added. The p-value is \emph{computed by this function} (see \code{\link[=.lrtPValue]{.lrtPValue()}}) from
the difference in -2*log-likelihood between the reduced and full model,
where the reduced/full roles are set by the step direction (forward: the
reference is the reduced model; backward: the tested model is the reduced
model) rather than by the likelihood values. \code{df} is the number of
coefficients the relationship adds (1 for a continuous covariate,
categories - 1 for a categorical covariate). The \code{Significant} flag uses
the \strong{direction-specific} LRT threshold from the settings (forward
threshold for forward steps, backward threshold for backward steps;
Monolix defaults are 0.05 and 0.01).
\item \strong{BICc}: no statistical test is done; an \code{Improved} flag reports whether
BICc decreased relative to the reference model (\code{dBICc < 0}).
}
